# Force one canonical URL per page (the .html version — matches every
# canonical tag, the sitemap, and every internal link on this site).
# Netlify serves .html files at their extensionless path automatically
# regardless of the "Pretty URLs" toggle, which was creating duplicate
# URLs for the same page (e.g. /contact and /contact.html both resolving)
# and tripping Search Console's "Page with redirect" indexing warning.
# These forced 301s make the extensionless path redirect to the .html
# canonical instead of silently serving duplicate content.
/sell                 /sell.html                  301!
/contact              /contact.html               301!
/shop                 /shop.html                  301!
/about                /about.html                 301!
/curbside             /curbside.html              301!
/pokemon-tcg          /pokemon-tcg.html           301!
/one-piece-tcg        /one-piece-tcg.html         301!
/sports-cards         /sports-cards.html          301!
/toys-collectibles    /toys-collectibles.html     301!
/disney-lorcana       /disney-lorcana.html        301!
/goat-slabs           /goat-slabs.html            301!
/trading-card-games   /trading-card-games.html    301!
